    catholicResponse: "Catholic teaching agrees that the Magisterium is under and serves God's Word, not over it. The disagreement concerns how Christ willed the apostolic Gospel to remain identifiable and authoritatively interpreted. The New Testament itself is received within apostolic teaching, worship, and ordered transmission. Catholicism therefore sees Scripture and apostolic Tradition as inseparable modes of one deposit and the Magisterium as its servant interpreter, not as competing revelations. Later lessons must examine canon, succession, and particular definitions rather than treating this introductory synthesis as a complete proof.",
